// autodiff/ — reverse-mode automatic differentiation over a recorded tape.
//
// Depends on core alone. A Tape[A] holds the values and the closures that
// produced them; primitives push an entry per operation and the backward pass
// walks the tape in reverse accumulating adjoints. Nothing in that needs a
// tensor type, a parameter block or an optimiser -- autodiff_prims.mbt
// deliberately splits its operations into small bundles so a caller only pays
// for the generic machinery it uses.
//
// It sits below nn/ rather than beside it, which is the point: nn/'s layers
// hand-write their backward passes (conv2d_backward.mbt, linear_backward.mbt)
// because those are analytic and much cheaper than a tape. This package is for
// the cases where an analytic gradient is not worth deriving by hand.
//
// causal/ depends on this one: do_calculus and counterfactual_reasoning
// differentiate through an intervention graph, and autodiff_tape is how they do
// it without writing the chain rule out for every estimator.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
}
